    "description": "Pressed Glass Insulators Set - 2 Pieces\nHemingray, Multi-Pattern\nAqua and Straw, Vintage Antique\nThis collection features two distinct vintage glass insulators produced by Hemingray, a primary manufacturer of American telegraph and telephone insulators during the late 19th and early 20th centuries. These pieces represent the industrial history of communication, highly valued by collectors for their varied colors, embossed markings, and heavy glass construction.\nPieces Included:\nHemingray 680 Insulator, straw/clear color, top-mount design with triple-ribbed base, embossed \"HEMINGRAY - 680\" on the skirt\nHemingray Signal Insulator, aqua blue glass, beehive shape, embossed \"PATD NOV 13TH 1883\" on the base skirt\nCondition:\nThe aqua insulator shows standard age-related surface scuffs and minor internal bubbling consistent with period glass production; no major cracks or large chips are observed. The straw-colored 680 insulator exhibits surface cloudiness and some mineral deposits from outdoor exposure, but retains crisp embossed lettering. Both pieces are heavy and structurally sound for display.\nWarehouse Location: Cleveland\nDue to our lighting, white glare lines may appear on items - This is NOT damage\nIf you have any questions regarding the quality or authenticity of this item or general questions regarding and item, please click Contact Seller on the item page and send us a message. We are available to answer your questions Monday through Friday, 8 am - 3:00 pm, EST.\n* For combined shipping policy see the shipping tab.\nSome items may contain unseen flaws not noted in the description.\nSee Photos. Items sold as-is.",
